#### Copy text

¬TDOD 111 Copy text

Vscode_CodeSpellChecker_File_5

### Copy a word

1. **Select the word** using any of these methods:

   - **Drag cursor**  
     Place the mouse pointer just before the first letter of the word.  
     Press and hold the left mouse button.  
     Drag the pointer across the word to just after the last letter.  
     Release the mouse button.  
     The word is now highlighted.  
     > If you drag too far, you may select extra spaces or punctuation.  
     > If you don’t drag far enough, only part of the word will be selected.

   - **Double-click**  
     Double-click the word.

   - **Keyboard**  
     Place the cursor next to the word, then press `Ctrl+Shift+→` or `Ctrl+Shift+←`  
     (Windows/Linux) or `Option+Shift+→` / `Option+Shift+←` (macOS).

2. **Copy the selected word** using any of these methods:

   - **Keyboard shortcut**  
     `Ctrl+C` (Windows/Linux) or `Cmd+C` (macOS).  
     Alternative on Windows: `Ctrl+Insert`.

   - **Context menu**  
     Right-click the selected word, then choose **Copy**.

   - **Edit menu**  
     Go to **Edit > Copy**.

   - **Command Palette** *(VS Code)*  
     Press `Ctrl+Shift+P` (Windows/Linux) or `Cmd+Shift+P` (macOS),  
     type `Copy`, then select **Copy**.